---
import Callout from "../../components/Callout.astro";
import InlineCommand from "../../components/InlineCommand";
import PageShell from "../../components/PageShell.astro";
import TerminalBlock from "../../components/TerminalBlock";
import MainLayout from "../../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
---

<MainLayout title="Documentation - AI Training Guide">
  <PageShell chapterId="practical-exercise" subChapterId="documentation">
    <div class="prose space-y-6">

      <p>
        You've built features, reviewed diffs, created PRs, and validated against acceptance criteria. The last step is documentation. AI can generate the "what" quickly, but the "why" behind your technical choices still needs to come from you.
      </p>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-stone-800 mt-8 mb-4">Exercise 1: Generate Project Documentation</h2>
        <p>
          Have the AI generate a documentation page for the features you implemented during this training. The goal isn't a polished public-facing document. It's an internal reference that a teammate (or your future self) could use to understand what was built and how it works.
        </p>

        <div class="relative border-l-4 border-teal-400 pl-6 py-2 my-10">
          <div class="absolute -left-4 top-2 w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-teal-500 text-white text-sm font-bold flex items-center justify-center">1</div>
          <h3 class="mt-0 mb-2">Generate a First Draft</h3>
          <p class="text-stone-600 text-sm mb-4">
            Open a fresh chat and ask the AI to document the features you've built. Point it at the relevant source files so it has real context to work from.
          </p>
          <TerminalBlock
            title="Example Prompt"
            lines={[
              { type: "command", command: "Generate a technical documentation page for the features in this project. Cover the Habit Tracker, Pomodoro Timer, and any other features I've implemented. For each feature, describe what it does, the key components and hooks involved, and how data is stored. Write it as a markdown file at docs/features.md." },
            ]}
            client:visible
          />
        </div>

        <div class="relative border-l-4 border-teal-400 pl-6 py-2 my-10">
          <div class="absolute -left-4 top-2 w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-teal-500 text-white text-sm font-bold flex items-center justify-center">2</div>
          <h3 class="mt-0 mb-2">Review and Add Context</h3>
          <p class="text-stone-600 text-sm mb-4">
            Read through the generated documentation. The AI will do a reasonable job describing the code structure, but it won't know <em>why</em> you made certain decisions. Add context where it matters:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-stone-600">
            <li><strong>Tradeoffs:</strong> Why did you choose localStorage over a different storage approach? Why this component structure instead of an alternative?</li>
            <li><strong>Known limitations:</strong> What doesn't the feature handle? What would need to change if requirements grew?</li>
            <li><strong>Things that surprised you:</strong> Did the AI make a choice during implementation that you kept but found unexpected? Document why you kept it.</li>
          </ul>

          <Callout variant="tip" title="The AI Writes the What, You Add the Why">
            <p>
              This is a pattern you'll use repeatedly. AI is good at surveying code and summarizing structure. It's less good at capturing intent, constraints, and decisions that happened outside the code. Your review pass turns a generated summary into genuinely useful documentation.
            </p>
          </Callout>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-stone-800 mt-8 mb-4">Exercise 2: Update AGENTS.md</h2>
        <p>
          Throughout this training, you've added libraries, established patterns, and built features. Your <InlineCommand command="AGENTS.md" client:visible /> file should reflect the current state of the project so that future AI sessions have accurate context.
        </p>

        <div class="relative border-l-4 border-teal-400 pl-6 py-2 my-10">
          <div class="absolute -left-4 top-2 w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-teal-500 text-white text-sm font-bold flex items-center justify-center">1</div>
          <h3 class="mt-0 mb-2">Audit the Current File</h3>
          <p class="text-stone-600 text-sm mb-4">
            Start by reading the existing AGENTS.md and comparing it to the current state of the codebase.
          </p>
          <TerminalBlock
            title="Example Prompt"
            lines={[
              { type: "command", command: "Read @AGENTS.md and compare it to the current codebase. Identify anything that's outdated, missing, or inaccurate. List the gaps but don't make changes yet." },
            ]}
            client:visible
          />
        </div>

        <div class="relative border-l-4 border-teal-400 pl-6 py-2 my-10">
          <div class="absolute -left-4 top-2 w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-teal-500 text-white text-sm font-bold flex items-center justify-center">2</div>
          <h3 class="mt-0 mb-2">Update It</h3>
          <p class="text-stone-600 text-sm mb-4">
            Review the AI's gap analysis, then have it update the file. Focus on information that would help a future AI session (or a new teammate) work effectively in this codebase:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-stone-600">
            <li>New libraries or tools you added</li>
            <li>Patterns you established (component structure, state management, naming conventions)</li>
            <li>Files or directories that were created during development</li>
            <li>Any gotchas or constraints a future session should know about</li>
          </ul>
          <TerminalBlock
            title="Example Prompt"
            lines={[
              { type: "command", command: "Update @AGENTS.md with the gaps you identified. Keep the existing structure and tone. Don't remove anything that's still accurate." },
            ]}
            client:visible
          />
        </div>

        <div class="relative border-l-4 border-teal-400 pl-6 py-2 my-10">
          <div class="absolute -left-4 top-2 w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-teal-500 text-white text-sm font-bold flex items-center justify-center">3</div>
          <h3 class="mt-0 mb-2">Review the Changes</h3>
          <p class="text-stone-600 text-sm mb-4">
            Read the diff. AGENTS.md is read by every future AI session, so accuracy matters. Verify that:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-stone-600">
            <li>Library versions and tool references are correct</li>
            <li>Described patterns match what's actually in the code</li>
            <li>Nothing was removed that's still relevant</li>
            <li>The file isn't bloated with obvious information the AI can infer from the code itself</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-stone-800 mt-8 mb-4">What Good AI-Assisted Documentation Looks Like</h2>
        <p>
          Documentation generated with AI tends to be thorough on structure and thin on reasoning. A good documentation workflow with AI follows a pattern:
        </p>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 my-6">
          <div class="bg-teal-50 border border-teal-200 rounded-lg p-5">
            <h4 class="text-teal-800 font-bold mt-0 mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
              <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-teal-500"></span>
              AI Generates
            </h4>
            <ul class="text-sm text-teal-900 leading-relaxed space-y-1 list-disc pl-4">
              <li>Feature summaries from source code</li>
              <li>Component and hook inventories</li>
              <li>Data flow descriptions</li>
              <li>API surface documentation</li>
              <li>File structure overviews</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-amber-50 border border-amber-200 rounded-lg p-5">
            <h4 class="text-amber-800 font-bold mt-0 mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
              <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-amber-500"></span>
              You Add
            </h4>
            <ul class="text-sm text-amber-900 leading-relaxed space-y-1 list-disc pl-4">
              <li>Why this approach over alternatives</li>
              <li>Known limitations and constraints</li>
              <li>Context from discussions or decisions</li>
              <li>Gotchas that aren't obvious from code</li>
              <li>Links to related tickets or specs</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="border-t border-stone-200 pt-8 mt-8">
        <p class="text-stone-800 font-medium">
          Commit your documentation and AGENTS.md updates. This closes the loop on the full development cycle: requirements, task breakdowns, implementation, validation, PR creation, and documentation, all AI-assisted but human-directed.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </PageShell>
</MainLayout>
